## Provenance

The 53 original questions were generated with ChatGPT at the maintainer's direction as the project's initial practice set, establishing its original format and style. They were not sourced from an actual certification exam, a third-party question bank, a course, or any other existing practice material. They were subsequently independently audited for technical accuracy against current first-party documentation and maintained as part of this project going forward; see `docs/audits/legacy-question-audit.md` for that audit record.

The 318 expanded-bank questions were authored and reviewed separately, each against current first-party technical documentation (see [docs/question-bank-methodology.md](docs/question-bank-methodology.md) for the process, and `sourceRefs` on each question for the specific sources).

This describes where the content came from, not a claim that it's necessarily unique — generated or independently written practice material covering the same publicly documented technical concepts could plausibly exist elsewhere, written differently. It's also not a claim of any affiliation with Anthropic or Pearson VUE; see the disclaimer in [README.md](README.md).
